searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"Msutils.Data.Types","doc":"Data types  for the mscmp_syst_utils_data component.","ref":"Msutils.Data.Types.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Msutils.Data.Types.common_validators/0","doc":"Establishes the known common changeset validator options.","ref":"Msutils.Data.Types.html#t:common_validators/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Msutils.Data","doc":"This is a set of utilities for working with data which is generally\nuseful across components.\n\nCurrently included in these utilities are:\n\n* ETS operations\n\n  Functions wrap some typical ETS operations so that they return standard result\n  tuples.\n\n* Changeset validators\n\n  Common validation functions which can be used to validate changesets across\n  Components.\n\n<!-- MDESC !-->\n\n> #### Note {: .info}\n>\n> `Changeset Validators` do not check their `opts` parameter for validity.  This\n> is expected to be handled by the caller prior to calling these functions.  See\n> the `Msutils.Data.common_validator_options/1` macro for more information on\n> adding the standard options which can be used to validate changesets.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Data.validate_display_name/2","doc":"Changeset validation ensuring that the `display_name` field is valid and\nmeets minimum and maximum length requirements.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_display_name/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Data.validate_display_name/2","doc":"* `changeset` - an `Ecto.Changeset` struct to be validated.\n\n  * `opts` - options which configure the validation checks of the functions.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_display_name/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Msutils.Data.validate_display_name/2","doc":"* `:min_display_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of display_name values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_display_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of display_name values. The default value is `64`.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_display_name/2-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Data.validate_external_name/2","doc":"Changeset validation ensuring that the `external_name` field is valid and\nmeets minimum and maximum length requirements.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_external_name/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Data.validate_external_name/2","doc":"* `changeset` - an `Ecto.Changeset` struct to be validated.\n\n  * `opts` - options which configure the validation checks of the functions.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_external_name/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Msutils.Data.validate_external_name/2","doc":"* `:min_external_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of external_name values. The default value is `2`.\n\n* `:max_external_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of external_name values. The default value is `64`.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_external_name/2-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Data.validate_internal_name/2","doc":"Changeset validation ensuring that the `internal_name` field is valid and\nmeets minimum and maximum length requirements.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_internal_name/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Data.validate_internal_name/2","doc":"* `changeset` - an `Ecto.Changeset` struct to be validated.\n\n  * `opts` - options which configure the validation checks of the functions.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_internal_name/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Msutils.Data.validate_internal_name/2","doc":"* `:min_internal_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of internal_name values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_internal_name_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of internal_name values. The default value is `64`.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_internal_name/2-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Data.validate_syst_defined_changes/2","doc":"Changeset validation ensuring that, if the record is set as `syst_defined`,\nthe prohibited fields are not changed.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_syst_defined_changes/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Data.validate_syst_defined_changes/2","doc":"* `changeset` - an `Ecto.Changeset` struct to be validated.\n\n  * `prohibited_fields` - a list of field names for which changes are\n    prohibited if the record is set as `syst_defined`.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_syst_defined_changes/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Data.validate_user_description/2","doc":"Changeset validation ensuring that the `user_description` field is set if\nrequired and allowed and meets minimum and maximum length requirements.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_user_description/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Data.validate_user_description/2","doc":"* `changeset` - an `Ecto.Changeset` struct to be validated.\n\n  * `opts` - options which configure the validation checks of the functions.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_user_description/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Msutils.Data.validate_user_description/2","doc":"* `:min_user_description_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the minimum grapheme length of user_description values. The default value is `6`.\n\n* `:max_user_description_length` (`t:pos_integer/0`) - Sets the maximum grapheme length of user_description values. The default value is `1000`.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#validate_user_description/2-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Data.ets_delete/2","doc":"Deletes an entry from an ETS table.\n\nWraps the ETS `:ets.delete/2` function.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_delete/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Data.ets_delete/2","doc":"* `table` - the ETS table to delete from\n  * `key` - the key of the entry to delete","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_delete/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Msutils.Data.ets_delete/2","doc":"* `:ok` - if the deletion was successful\n  * `{:error, Mserror.DataUtilsError.t()}` - if there was an error during deletion","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_delete/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Data.ets_insert/2","doc":"Inserts data into an ETS table.\n\nIn this we wrap the ETS `:ets.insert/2` function in a function that returns\nan Mserror.DataUtilsError if there is an error.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_insert/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Data.ets_insert/2","doc":"* `table` - the ETS table to insert the data into.\n\n  * `data` - the data to insert into the ETS table.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_insert/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Msutils.Data.ets_insert/2","doc":"* `:ok` - if the data was successfully inserted into the ETS table.\n\n  * `{:error, Mserror.DataUtilsError.t()}` - if there was an error inserting\n    the data into the ETS table.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_insert/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Data.ets_lookup_element/3","doc":"Looks up an element in an ETS table by key and position.\n\nWraps the ETS `:ets.lookup_element/3` function, returning a result tuple.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_lookup_element/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Data.ets_lookup_element/3","doc":"* `table` - the ETS table to look up the element in\n  * `key` - the key to look up\n  * `element_index` - the position of the element to return","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_lookup_element/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Msutils.Data.ets_lookup_element/3","doc":"* `{:ok, term()}` - the element was found at the specified position\n  * `{:error, Mserror.DataUtilsError.t()}` - if there was an error during lookup","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_lookup_element/3-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Data.ets_update_element/3","doc":"Updates an element in an ETS table.\n\nWraps the ETS `:ets.update_element/3` function.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_update_element/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Data.ets_update_element/3","doc":"* `table` - the ETS table to update\n  * `key` - the key of the element to update\n  * `updated_data` - the new data to set","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_update_element/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Msutils.Data.ets_update_element/3","doc":"* `:ok` - if the update was successful\n  * `{:error, Mserror.DataUtilsError.t()}` - if there was an error during update","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#ets_update_element/3-returns"},{"type":"macro","title":"Msutils.Data.common_validator_options/1","doc":"Returns a NimbleOptions struct with the requested common validator options for\nuse with the Changeset validation functions from the Msutils.Data module.\n\nThe common validator options establish cross-Component standards for data\nlimits such as minimum and maximum lengths commonly used data fields.  In many\nways, these options act as constants for common Changeset validations.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#common_validator_options/1"},{"type":"macro","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Data.common_validator_options/1","doc":"* `selected_options` - selects the desired options from the common validator\n    option definitions.  This is in the form of a list of the desired options.","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#common_validator_options/1-parameters"},{"type":"macro","title":"Select Options - Msutils.Data.common_validator_options/1","doc":"The following are accepted for selected options:\n\n  * `:internal_name`\n\n  * `:display_name`\n\n  * `:external_name`\n\n  * `:user_description`","ref":"Msutils.Data.html#common_validator_options/1-select-options"},{"type":"exception","title":"Mserror.DataUtilsError","doc":"This module defines the macro related error types for the Msutils.Data module.","ref":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.kinds/0","doc":"Represents the available Kinds of error allowed by this Error type.","ref":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.html#t:kinds/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Available Kinds - Mserror.DataUtilsError.kinds/0","doc":"* `:macro` - Indicates that there were compilation errors in the macros provided by\nthis Component.  This will often times be due to invalid parameters being\npassed to the macros.\n\n  * `:ets_operations` - Indicates that there was an error in an ETS operation.","ref":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.html#t:kinds/0-available-kinds"},{"type":"type","title":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.t/0","doc":"Describes the structure of an error of generated by this exception.\n\nThe `cause` attribute allows for errors to be nested.","ref":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Attributes - Mserror.DataUtilsError.t/0","doc":"The following attributes are those which are set or modified by the\nuser when working with errors.\n\n  * `kind` - The kind of error, see `t:kinds/0` for the available Kinds.\n\n  * `message` - A string describing the error.\n\n  * `context` - contextual information for better understanding the\n    error.  If provided, the context should be of type\n    `t:MscmpSystError.Types.Context.t/0`.\n\n  * `cause` - The cause of the error, which can be an exception, an error tuple,\n    or any other term.","ref":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.html#t:t/0-attributes"},{"type":"type","title":"Internal Attributes - Mserror.DataUtilsError.t/0","doc":"These attributes have their values set at compile time and are used\ninternally by the MscmpSystError framework.  They are not to be altered\nby user code.  Reading these attributes in user code is safe, however.\n\n  * `__mserror__` - Always true, indicates that this error is compatible\n    with the MscmpSystError framework.\n\n  * `__mscomponent__` - The component that generated the error.","ref":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.html#t:t/0-internal-attributes"},{"type":"function","title":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.new/3","doc":"Creates a new error struct with the given kind, message, and options.","ref":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.html#new/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Mserror.DataUtilsError.new/3","doc":"* `kind` - The kind of error, see `t:kinds/0` for the available Kinds.\n\n  * `message` - A string describing the error.\n\n  * `opts` - A keyword list of additional options.","ref":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.html#new/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Mserror.DataUtilsError.new/3","doc":"* `:context` - contextual information for better understanding the\n    error.  If provided, the context should be of type\n    `t:MscmpSystError.Types.Context.t/0`.\n\n  * `:cause` - The cause of the error, which can be an exception, an error tuple,\n    or any other term.\n\n  * `:parse_error` - An error result conforming with\n    `t:MscmpSystError.Types.parsable_error/0` to be parsed overriding\n    certain attributes of the exception struct.  When provided the\n    `message` parameter is treated as a default message which can be\n    overridden by a message supplied by the error result provided to this\n    option.  The `cause` attribute of the exception struct will be set to\n    a value derived from this option's value, ignoring the `:cause`\n    option if provided; typically you would not provide both\n    `:parse_error` and `:cause` in the same call to `new/3`.","ref":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.html#new/3-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Mserror.DataUtilsError.new/3","doc":"Returns a struct of this error type with the error details.","ref":"Mserror.DataUtilsError.html#new/3-returns"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.38.4"}}